# Backend DDD Architecture

## Module Structure

Every bounded context follows this exact layout — never deviate:

```
internal/module/<name>/
  domain/       # Aggregate roots, entities, value objects, events, errors
  store/        # DB queries (wraps sqlc gen code)
  service/      # Application/use-case logic
  handler/      # HTTP handlers (Echo)
  api/          # Public API interface exposed to other modules
  module.go     # Wires deps, implements platform/module.Module
```

## Aggregate Roots

Current ARs: `User` (IAM), `Transaction` (Wallet), `Order` (Trading).

- All mutations go through the AR's public methods — never modify internal entities directly
- Every state transition must call `a.raise(event)` to collect a domain event
- Once an AR is `completed`/`filled`/`reversed`/`cancelled`, it is **immutable** — no further transitions

```go
// ❌ BAD — mutating internal state directly
order.Status = domain.StatusFilled

// ✅ GOOD — through AR method that validates invariants and emits event
if err := order.Fill(qty); err != nil { ... }
```

## Domain Events

All events must implement:
```go
type DomainEvent interface {
    EventType()   string
    OccurredAt()  time.Time
    AggregateID() kernel.ID
}
```

- Events are collected in-memory on the AR during a command
- Events are dispatched **after** the DB transaction commits (outbox in Phase 1)
- Event type strings use `<context>.<past_tense>` format: `trading.order_placed`, `wallet.hold_settled`

## gen/sqlc — Read-Only

**Never edit files under `gen/sqlc/`** — they are regenerated by `make sqlc`.
Add or modify queries only in `sql/queries/<context>/*.sql`, then regenerate.
